// THE v1.3 WAVE — VERNACULAR LAW + LANE EXCISION (operator 2026-07-29):
//   OPERATOR: "all 5 locations must have consistent naming... one long spelled out
//   name and one and only one short hand version that strives for clarity not
//   brevity... naked is a fail because it can mean many things."
//   R1 EXCISED BDRB-09/10/11/12. PROVEN redundant, not merely noisy:
//     BDR_NAKED_J = PBJ and RC and RS and DIR and FD = PBJ and BDR_CORE = BDR_HC_J,
//     and BDR_ANY_J was ASSIGNED to BDR_HC_J — one boolean, three names. BDR_HC_*
//     contains DIR = rv_base*, and the four tiers partition rv_base* on rv_normPrice,
//     so exactly one of 01..04 fires on every bar where 09/11 fired. Zero information.
//     Operator's TV export (SHC 5m): 09 and 11 fired the IDENTICAL 3 bars, 0 XOR;
//     01(1)+02(2)=3=09(3)=11(3), both-fire 0, neither-fire 0.
//   R2 RESIDUALISED 01/05: NO-TIER = base and not KRATOS/SAAB and not RVOL-1X and
//     not MOAB/GS (was rv_norm < th_saab). Exhaustive BY CONSTRUCTION, so R1's proof
//     survives any future threshold edit.
//   R3 VERNACULAR — one typed record per lane, both names DERIVED, never typed:
//     LONG  = "{id} · {side} · {pocket}+KC-RC+KC-RS · {kind} {qualifier}"
//     SHORT = "{qualifier}\n{pocket}"
//     LONG on Style-tab title + plot checkbox + alert checkbox; SHORT on chart+alert.
//     Kills the unmarked-default defect: 01-04 printed "... / BDR" with NO pocket
//     token while 05-08 printed "... / BDR PB" — 8 lanes across the pair were
//     unreadable as PBJ-vs-PB. Clarity over brevity: KRATOS not KRAT, PENTHOUSE not PH.
//   R4 ALERT GRAMMAR v2: DP leftmost, then lane id, then session marker, then
//     DISP → RVOL-with-direction → HV. No ticker/interval/exchange.
//   R5 "ANY BEDROCK" retired — it denoted the BASE GATE while "+ ANY FABLE" denotes
//     a 28-member disjunction. Internal BDR_ANY_* renamed BDR_BASE_*.
// Gate: validation/wrappers/vernacular_gate.py (D_vern = 0).
// Version control: bedrock/CHANGELOG.md - github.com/nishpa800/indicators
