// THE v1.2 WAVE — FIRST-BAR MASTER BECOMES AN ALERT GATE (operator 2026-07-29):
//   ★ FIRST BAR MASTER ★ in v1.1 gated the DETECTION layer (sig_*), so ON killed
//     the VISUAL PLOTS off the first bar as well as the alerts. Operator law:
//     "we need to see the visual plots but if we check the first bar checkbox,
//     then and only then we ONLY want the alert if the first bar criteria is met".
//   TRANSFORM per lane L (c(L) = its reference-bar class fb0/fb1/fb01/fbs/fbm/fb12):
//     OLD  sig_L = D_L and c(L);  fire_L = en_L and sig_L;  alf_L = al_L and sig_L
//     NEW  sig_L = D_L;           fire_L = en_L and sig_L         <- PLOT, ungated
//          aok_L = sig_L and c(L);  alf_L = al_L and aok_L        <- ALERT, gated
//     qn term fire_L -> (en_L and aok_L)  [= old fire_L exactly, alert text invariant]
//   T-A alert invariance   alf_new = al and (D and hc) and c = alf_old (and comm/assoc)
//   T-B qn invariance      en and aok = en and sig_old = fire_old
//   T-C plot uncondition   fire_new carries no c term => independent of the master
//   T-D master-OFF ident   OFF => c == true => whole study identical to v1.1
//   T-E alert totality     every alf_L carries a c(L) factor. CLOSURES: S20/S21
//     (b2bFC two-bar B2B) get fb01; S32/S33 (OPEN1) get fb0 — a provable no-op,
//     det_open1* already requires is_new_sess. v1.1 left all four alert-ungated.
//   First-bar definition UNCHANGED and estate-canonical:
//     is_new_sess = is_new_day = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
//     (identical to FIRST BAR FABLE v3/EXT v6 and SECONDS v1; B2B PUP's
//      session.isfirstbar is the same boundary). NOT redefined here.
//   Plot budget UNCHANGED — no plotshape line is touched, only the boolean each
//   one already read (fire_*) is now first-bar-independent.
